/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL · 2 Kings chapters 11-15
   Verse text is filled/verified from the KJV by tools/fill-verses.js */
VG.registerBibleChapters("2kings", [
{n:11, name:"The Boy King", seal:{ref:"2 Kings 11:17",verse:"And Jehoiada made a covenant between the LORD and the king and the people that they should be the LORD’S people; between the king also and the people."}, facts:["Did you know the boy king Joash was hidden six years in the very house of the LORD, raised in the temple while Athaliah murdered the rest of the royal family (2 Kings 11:2-3)?","Did you know Jehoiada armed his captains with King David's own spears and shields, treasured in the temple for generations (2 Kings 11:10)?","Did you know Athaliah's last recorded words were a double cry of 'Treason, Treason,' even as all the people of the land rejoiced around the child king (2 Kings 11:14)?"], questions:[
{q:"What did Athaliah do when she saw that her son Ahaziah was dead?", options:["She arose and destroyed all the seed royal","She fled to Samaria for safety","She crowned herself in the temple","She made peace with the priests"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 11:1",verse:"And when Athaliah the mother of Ahaziah saw that her son was dead, she arose and destroyed all the seed royal.", insight:"Power that feeds on murder ends by devouring its own house; Athaliah's cruelty could not outlast God's promise to David."},
{q:"Who stole the infant Joash from among the king's sons who were slain?", options:["Jehosheba, the daughter of king Joram","Athaliah's own nurse","Jehoiada the priest himself","The captain of the guard"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 11:2",verse:"But Jehosheba, the daughter of king Joram, sister of Ahaziah, took Joash the son of Ahaziah and stole him from among the king’s sons which were slain; and they hid him, even him and his nurse, in the bedchamber from Athaliah, so that he was not slain.", insight:"One brave woman with a nurse saved the royal line; God often hides His greatest works in a bedchamber."},
{q:"Where did Jehosheba hide Joash and his nurse from Athaliah?", options:["In the bedchamber, then in the house of the LORD","In a cave in the wilderness","In the king's treasury","In a village of Judah"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 11:2",verse:"But Jehosheba, the daughter of king Joram, sister of Ahaziah, took Joash the son of Ahaziah and stole him from among the king’s sons which were slain; and they hid him, even him and his nurse, in the bedchamber from Athaliah, so that he was not slain.", insight:"A bedchamber became a throne room in waiting; God prepares kings in hidden places."},
{q:"How long was Joash hidden in the house of the LORD while Athaliah reigned?", options:["Six years","Three years","Twelve years","Forty years"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 11:3",verse:"And he was with her hid in the house of the LORD six years. And Athaliah did reign over the land.", insight:"Six years of silence while evil reigned; God is not idle when He seems hidden."},
{q:"In which year did Jehoiada send for the rulers over hundreds, the captains, and the guard?", options:["The seventh year","The first year","The third year","The fortieth year"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 11:4",verse:"And the seventh year Jehoiada sent and fetched the rulers over hundreds, with the captains and the guard, and brought them to him into the house of the LORD, and made a covenant with them, and took an oath of them in the house of the LORD, and shewed them the king’s son.", insight:"The seventh year came on God's calendar, not man's; wait for His timing, then move boldly."},
{q:"What did Jehoiada show the rulers in the house of the LORD?", options:["The king's son","The crown jewels","The book of the law","The ark of the covenant"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 11:4",verse:"And the seventh year Jehoiada sent and fetched the rulers over hundreds, with the captains and the guard, and brought them to him into the house of the LORD, and made a covenant with them, and took an oath of them in the house of the LORD, and shewed them the king’s son.", insight:"He bound the leaders by covenant and oath before revealing the king; godly plans rest on promises, not plots."},
{q:"What part of the sabbath guard was to keep the watch of the king's house?", options:["A third part of those entering on the sabbath","All of the guard together","The captains only","The Levites alone"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 11:5",verse:"And he commanded them, saying, This is the thing that ye shall do; A third part of you that enter in on the sabbath shall even be keepers of the watch of the king’s house;", insight:"Careful thirds and watches; wisdom plans the details when God's moment comes."},
{q:"At which two places were the other thirds of the guard posted?", options:["The gate of Sur and the gate behind the guard","The east gate and the west gate","The temple porch and the altar","The palace and the treasury"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 11:6",verse:"And a third part shall be at the gate of Sur; and a third part at the gate behind the guard: so shall ye keep the watch of the house, that it be not broken down.", insight:"Every gate guarded; the house of God was not to be broken down while the king was crowned."},
{q:"What were the two parts going forth on the sabbath to guard?", options:["The house of the LORD about the king","The city walls of Jerusalem","The road to Bethlehem","The storehouses of the temple"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 11:7",verse:"And two parts of all you that go forth on the sabbath, even they shall keep the watch of the house of the LORD about the king.", insight:"The king surrounded by loyal watchers; God's anointed are never truly alone."},
{q:"What was to happen to anyone who came within the ranges around the king?", options:["He was to be slain","He was to be arrested","He was to be blessed","He was to be ignored"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 11:8",verse:"And ye shall compass the king round about, every man with his weapons in his hand: and he that cometh within the ranges, let him be slain: and be ye with the king as he goeth out and as he cometh in.", insight:"Serious boundaries guarded the young king; reverence for God's chosen is not optional."},
{q:"With what weapons did Jehoiada arm the captains over hundreds?", options:["King David's spears and shields from the temple","New swords from Egypt","Bows from the armory","Slings and stones"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 11:10",verse:"And to the captains over hundreds did the priest give king David’s spears and shields, that were in the temple of the LORD.", insight:"David's old weapons armed a new generation; faith hands down its arms to its children."},
{q:"What two things were given to the king's son when they made him king?", options:["The crown and the testimony","The scepter and the sword","The ring and the robe","The throne and the treasury"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 11:12",verse:"And he brought forth the king’s son, and put the crown upon him, and gave him the testimony; and they made him king, and anointed him; and they clapped their hands, and said, God save the king.", insight:"Crown and testimony together; true kingship wears authority and obeys God's law."},
{q:"What did the people cry as Joash was anointed?", options:["God save the king","Long live the queen","Blessed be the LORD","Hosanna in the highest"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 11:12",verse:"And he brought forth the king’s son, and put the crown upon him, and gave him the testimony; and they made him king, and anointed him; and they clapped their hands, and said, God save the king.", insight:"'God save the king' was a prayer as much as a cheer; nations thrive when they ask God to save their rulers."},
{q:"Where did the young king stand, as the manner was?", options:["By a pillar","On the altar","In the holy place","At the east gate"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 11:14",verse:"And when she looked, behold, the king stood by a pillar, as the manner was, and the princes and the trumpeters by the king, and all the people of the land rejoiced, and blew with trumpets: and Athaliah rent her clothes, and cried, Treason, Treason.", insight:"The king stood by the pillar, as the manner was; God's order outlasts every usurper's fashion."},
{q:"What did Athaliah cry when she saw the young king crowned?", options:["Treason, Treason","Mercy, mercy","Murder, murder","Save me, save me"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 11:14",verse:"And when she looked, behold, the king stood by a pillar, as the manner was, and the princes and the trumpeters by the king, and all the people of the land rejoiced, and blew with trumpets: and Athaliah rent her clothes, and cried, Treason, Treason.", insight:"She cried 'Treason' while guilty of it; guilt often accuses others of its own sin."},
{q:"Why did Jehoiada order Athaliah taken outside the ranges?", options:["That she not be slain in the house of the LORD","To parade her through the city","To try her before the elders","To exile her to Samaria"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 11:15",verse:"But Jehoiada the priest commanded the captains of the hundreds, the officers of the host, and said unto them, Have her forth without the ranges: and him that followeth her kill with the sword. For the priest had said, Let her not be slain in the house of the LORD.", insight:"Even judgment respected the house of the LORD; holiness sets the terms, even for execution."},
{q:"By which way was Athaliah led out to her death?", options:["By the way the horses came into the king's house","Through the sheep gate","Down to the valley of Kidron","Across the Jordan"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 11:16",verse:"And they laid hands on her; and she went by the way by the which the horses came into the king’s house: and there was she slain.", insight:"Led out by the horses' way to die; the path of pride ends outside the house of God."},
{q:"What covenant did Jehoiada make that day?", options:["Between the LORD and the king and the people, that they should be the LORD's people","Between Judah and Israel","Between the priests and the guard","Between Joash and Athaliah's house"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 11:17",verse:"And Jehoiada made a covenant between the LORD and the king and the people that they should be the LORD’S people; between the king also and the people.", insight:"A nation renewed starts with a covenant: the LORD's people, bound to the LORD and to each other."},
{q:"What happened to the house of Baal?", options:["The people broke it down and slew Mattan the priest of Baal","It was turned into a palace","It was left standing empty","It was burned by the Syrians"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 11:18",verse:"And all the people of the land went into the house of Baal, and brake it down; his altars and his images brake they in pieces thoroughly, and slew Mattan the priest of Baal before the altars. And the priest appointed officers over the house of the LORD.", insight:"Baal's house fell the same day the true king rose; revival always topples the idols."},
{q:"How old was Jehoash when he began to reign?", options:["Seven years old","Twelve years old","Sixteen years old","Thirty years old"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 11:21",verse:"Seven years old was Jehoash when he began to reign.", insight:"Seven years old and on the throne; God does not need our strength to keep His promises."}
]},
{n:12, name:"Repairing the Temple", seal:{ref:"2 Kings 12:2",verse:"And Jehoash did that which was right in the sight of the LORD all his days wherein Jehoiada the priest instructed him."}, facts:["Did you know Jehoiada's chest with a hole bored in its lid, set beside the altar, was the first offering box in Scripture (2 Kings 12:9)?","Did you know the repair funds were handled with such honesty that no accounting was kept: 'they reckoned not with the men... for they dealt faithfully' (2 Kings 12:15)?","Did you know Jehoash, who repaired God's house, later stripped it of gold to buy off Hazael of Syria, and died by the swords of his own servants (2 Kings 12:18, 20)?"], questions:[
{q:"How long did Jehoash reign in Jerusalem?", options:["Forty years","Twenty nine years","Fifty two years","Sixteen years"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 12:1",verse:"In the seventh year of Jehu Jehoash began to reign; and forty years reigned he in Jerusalem. And his mother’s name was Zibiah of Beer-sheba.", insight:"Forty years is a long mercy; length of reign is no proof of a right heart to the end."},
{q:"Who was the mother of Jehoash?", options:["Zibiah of Beer-sheba","Jehosheba of Jerusalem","Jehoaddan of Jerusalem","Athaliah of Samaria"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 12:1",verse:"In the seventh year of Jehu Jehoash began to reign; and forty years reigned he in Jerusalem. And his mother’s name was Zibiah of Beer-sheba.", insight:"Zibiah of Beer-sheba is named and remembered; God records the mothers behind the kings."},
{q:"What marked all the days of Jehoash's good reign?", options:["The days wherein Jehoiada the priest instructed him","The years of peace with Syria","The building of new cities","The alliance with Israel"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 12:2",verse:"And Jehoash did that which was right in the sight of the LORD all his days wherein Jehoiada the priest instructed him.", insight:"He did right while Jehoiada instructed him; borrowed faith lasts only as long as the teacher."},
{q:"What did Jehoash fail to take away?", options:["The high places","The groves of Asherah","The idols of Baal","The temple tax"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 12:3",verse:"But the high places were not taken away: the people still sacrificed and burnt incense in the high places.", insight:"The high places stayed; a half reformation leaves the old altars smoking."},
{q:"What money did Jehoash set apart for the temple?", options:["All the money of the dedicated things brought into the house of the LORD","Only the king's own silver","The tribute from Syria","The wages of the priests"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 12:4",verse:"And Jehoash said to the priests, All the money of the dedicated things that is brought into the house of the LORD, even the money of every one that passeth the account, the money that every man is set at, and all the money that cometh into any man’s heart to bring into the house of the LORD,", insight:"Dedicated money for a dedicated house; giving that is set apart should stay set apart."},
{q:"What were the priests to do with the money?", options:["Repair the breaches of the house wherever any breach was found","Buy new vessels of gold","Pay the singers","Build the king a palace"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 12:5",verse:"Let the priests take it to them, every man of his acquaintance: and let them repair the breaches of the house, wheresoever any breach shall be found.", insight:"Repair the breaches wherever found; God's house deserves our first care, not our leftovers."},
{q:"In what year of Jehoash had the priests still not repaired the breaches?", options:["The three and twentieth year","The seventh year","The fortieth year","The twelfth year"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 12:6",verse:"But it was so, that in the three and twentieth year of king Jehoash the priests had not repaired the breaches of the house.", insight:"Twenty three years and nothing repaired; trusted men can still neglect the work."},
{q:"What did Jehoash ask the priests?", options:["Why repair ye not the breaches of the house?","Where is the ark of the covenant?","Who stole the temple gold?","When will ye anoint my son?"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 12:7",verse:"Then king Jehoash called for Jehoiada the priest, and the other priests, and said unto them, Why repair ye not the breaches of the house? now therefore receive no more money of your acquaintance, but deliver it for the breaches of the house.", insight:"'Why repair ye not?' A good king asks the hard question of his own priests."},
{q:"What did Jehoiada set beside the altar to receive the money?", options:["A chest with a hole bored in the lid","A golden basin","A silver trumpet","A brazen altar"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 12:9",verse:"But Jehoiada the priest took a chest, and bored a hole in the lid of it, and set it beside the altar, on the right side as one cometh into the house of the LORD: and the priests that kept the door put therein all the money that was brought into the house of the LORD.", insight:"A chest with a hole in the lid; sometimes the simplest system is the most honest one."},
{q:"Where exactly was the chest placed?", options:["Beside the altar, on the right side as one enters the house of the LORD","In the holy of holies","At the east gate","In the king's chamber"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 12:9",verse:"But Jehoiada the priest took a chest, and bored a hole in the lid of it, and set it beside the altar, on the right side as one cometh into the house of the LORD: and the priests that kept the door put therein all the money that was brought into the house of the LORD.", insight:"Set beside the altar on the right as one enters; giving belongs near worship, not far from it."},
{q:"When the chest held much money, who came up to count it?", options:["The king's scribe and the high priest","Jehoiada alone","The captains of the guard","The Levites"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 12:10",verse:"And it was so, when they saw that there was much money in the chest, that the king’s scribe and the high priest came up, and they put up in bags, and told the money that was found in the house of the LORD.", insight:"The scribe and the high priest counted together; money for God deserves two sets of eyes."},
{q:"Into whose hands was the counted money given?", options:["Them that did the work, that had the oversight of the house","The priests of the high places","The merchants of Tyre","The king's own treasury"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 12:11",verse:"And they gave the money, being told, into the hands of them that did the work, that had the oversight of the house of the LORD: and they laid it out to the carpenters and builders, that wrought upon the house of the LORD,", insight:"Paid straight to the workmen with oversight; honest labor deserves honest wages."},
{q:"Which workmen are named in the repairs?", options:["Carpenters, builders, masons, and hewers of stone","Goldsmiths and weavers","Potters and bakers","Scribes and singers"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 12:12",verse:"And to masons, and hewers of stone, and to buy timber and hewed stone to repair the breaches of the house of the LORD, and for all that was laid out for the house to repair it.", insight:"Masons, hewers, timber, stone; God's work needs many hands and real materials."},
{q:"What was not made from the repair money?", options:["Bowls of silver, snuffers, basons, trumpets, or vessels of gold and silver","Timber and hewed stone","Wages for the workmen","Repairs to the breaches"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 12:13",verse:"Howbeit there were not made for the house of the LORD bowls of silver, snuffers, basons, trumpets, any vessels of gold, or vessels of silver, of the money that was brought into the house of the LORD:", insight:"No showy vessels from the repair fund; the building came before the ornaments."},
{q:"Why was no account kept with the workmen?", options:["For they dealt faithfully","They were few in number","The king trusted only Jehoiada","The money was too little"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 12:15",verse:"Moreover they reckoned not with the men, into whose hand they delivered the money to be bestowed on workmen: for they dealt faithfully.", insight:"'They dealt faithfully' is the highest audit; character is the best accounting."},
{q:"What money was kept by the priests and not brought into the house?", options:["The trespass money and sin money","The dedicated silver","The census money","The firstfruits"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 12:16",verse:"The trespass money and sin money was not brought into the house of the LORD: it was the priests’.", insight:"Trespass and sin money stayed with the priests; even in reform, God's order for His ministers stood."},
{q:"Which city did Hazael take before setting his face toward Jerusalem?", options:["Gath","Gaza","Lachish","Megiddo"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 12:17",verse:"Then Hazael king of Syria went up, and fought against Gath, and took it: and Hazael set his face to go up to Jerusalem.", insight:"Hazael took Gath and set his face toward Jerusalem; small surrenders invite larger threats."},
{q:"How did Jehoash turn Hazael away from Jerusalem?", options:["He sent him all the dedicated gold of the temple and the king's house","He met him in battle at Gath","He hired Egyptian mercenaries","He hid the treasures in the wilderness"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 12:18",verse:"And Jehoash king of Judah took all the hallowed things that Jehoshaphat, and Jehoram, and Ahaziah, his fathers, kings of Judah, had dedicated, and his own hallowed things, and all the gold that was found in the treasures of the house of the LORD, and in the king’s house, and sent it to Hazael king of Syria: and he went away from Jerusalem.", insight:"He stripped God's house to pay Syria; what we refuse to trust God with, we end up losing anyway."},
{q:"Where was Joash slain by his conspiring servants?", options:["In the house of Millo, which goeth down to Silla","In the temple court","On the road to Lachish","In the palace at Samaria"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 12:20",verse:"And his servants arose, and made a conspiracy, and slew Joash in the house of Millo, which goeth down to Silla.", insight:"Conspiracy in the house of Millo; the king who forgot the temple's God fell to his own servants."},
{q:"Which two servants smote Joash?", options:["Jozachar the son of Shimeath, and Jehozabad the son of Shomer","Mattan and Shebna","Zabad and Jehozabad of Moab","The sons of Athaliah"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 12:21",verse:"For Jozachar the son of Shimeath, and Jehozabad the son of Shomer, his servants, smote him, and he died; and they buried him with his fathers in the city of David: and Amaziah his son reigned in his stead.", insight:"Jozachar and Jehozabad are named; God does not forget the hands that strike His anointed, even a failing one."}
]},
{n:13, name:"Elisha's Last Arrow", seal:{ref:"2 Kings 13:23",verse:"And the LORD was gracious unto them, and had compassion on them, and had respect unto them, because of his covenant with Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob, and would not destroy them, neither cast he them from his presence as yet."}, facts:["Did you know King Joash wept over the dying Elisha with the very words Elisha had cried over Elijah: 'O my father, my father, the chariot of Israel, and the horsemen thereof' (2 Kings 13:14)?","Did you know a dead man came back to life when his body touched Elisha's bones, the prophet's last miracle, performed after his death (2 Kings 13:21)?","Did you know Syria had reduced Israel's army to fifty horsemen, ten chariots, and ten thousand footmen, made 'like the dust by threshing' (2 Kings 13:7)?"], questions:[
{q:"How many years did Jehoahaz reign over Israel in Samaria?", options:["Seventeen years","Sixteen years","Forty one years","Twenty nine years"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 13:1",verse:"In the three and twentieth year of Joash the son of Ahaziah king of Judah Jehoahaz the son of Jehu began to reign over Israel in Samaria, and reigned seventeen years.", insight:"Seventeen years of an evil reign; time is no excuse when the pattern is sin."},
{q:"Whose sins did Jehoahaz follow?", options:["Jeroboam the son of Nebat","Ahab the son of Omri","The Baal of the Sidonians","The kings of Judah"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 13:2",verse:"And he did that which was evil in the sight of the LORD, and followed the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, which made Israel to sin; he departed not therefrom.", insight:"He followed Jeroboam's sins and never departed; inherited sin becomes chosen sin when we stay in it."},
{q:"Into whose hands did the LORD deliver Israel?", options:["Hazael king of Syria, and Ben-hadad his son","Pul and Tiglath-pileser","The Philistines and Moabites","Pharaoh of Egypt"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 13:3",verse:"And the anger of the LORD was kindled against Israel, and he delivered them into the hand of Hazael king of Syria, and into the hand of Ben-hadad the son of Hazael, all their days.", insight:"Delivered into Syria's hand all their days; persistent sin brings persistent sorrow."},
{q:"What did Jehoahaz do when Syria oppressed Israel?", options:["He besought the LORD","He fled to Judah","He paid tribute to Egypt","He rebuilt the groves"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 13:4",verse:"And Jehoahaz besought the LORD, and the LORD hearkened unto him: for he saw the oppression of Israel, because the king of Syria oppressed them.", insight:"Even an evil king's prayer was heard; God answers the cry of the oppressed, whoever cries."},
{q:"What did the LORD give Israel in answer to Jehoahaz's prayer?", options:["A saviour, so they went out from under the hand of the Syrians","A new king in Samaria","Rain after three years","A wall around Jerusalem"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 13:5",verse:"(And the LORD gave Israel a saviour, so that they went out from under the hand of the Syrians: and the children of Israel dwelt in their tents, as beforetime.", insight:"God gave a saviour, not because they deserved it, but because they were His."},
{q:"What idolatrous thing still remained in Samaria after the deliverance?", options:["The grove","The golden calves at Dan","The altar of Baal","The high place at Gibeon"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 13:6",verse:"Nevertheless they departed not from the sins of the house of Jeroboam, who made Israel sin, but walked therein: and there remained the grove also in Samaria.)", insight:"The grove remained in Samaria; deliverance without repentance leaves the idols standing."},
{q:"How many horsemen did Syria leave to Jehoahaz?", options:["Fifty horsemen","Five hundred horsemen","Five thousand horsemen","No horsemen at all"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 13:7",verse:"Neither did he leave of the people to Jehoahaz but fifty horsemen, and ten chariots, and ten thousand footmen; for the king of Syria had destroyed them, and had made them like the dust by threshing.", insight:"Fifty horsemen left of an army; sin had threshed Israel like dust."},
{q:"What had the king of Syria made Israel's army like?", options:["Like the dust by threshing","Like chaff before the wind","Like broken pottery","Like a scattered flock"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 13:7",verse:"Neither did he leave of the people to Jehoahaz but fifty horsemen, and ten chariots, and ten thousand footmen; for the king of Syria had destroyed them, and had made them like the dust by threshing.", insight:"Made like the dust by threshing; when God is not our strength, enemies thresh us."},
{q:"How long did Jehoash the son of Jehoahaz reign over Israel?", options:["Sixteen years","Seventeen years","Forty one years","Six months"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 13:10",verse:"In the thirty and seventh year of Joash king of Judah began Jehoash the son of Jehoahaz to reign over Israel in Samaria, and reigned sixteen years.", insight:"Sixteen more years of the same evil; a new king does not mean a new heart."},
{q:"What did King Joash cry, weeping over the dying Elisha?", options:["O my father, my father, the chariot of Israel, and the horsemen thereof","O prophet of God, do not leave us","Bless me before thou diest","Heal thyself, man of God"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 13:14",verse:"Now Elisha was fallen sick of his sickness whereof he died. And Joash the king of Israel came down unto him, and wept over his face, and said, O my father, my father, the chariot of Israel, and the horsemen thereof.", insight:"The king wept over the dying prophet; even godless men feel the loss of God's voice."},
{q:"What did Elisha tell the king to take?", options:["Bow and arrows","Sword and shield","Sackcloth and ashes","Oil and a cruse"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 13:15",verse:"And Elisha said unto him, Take bow and arrows. And he took unto him bow and arrows.", insight:"Take bow and arrows; God's victories still require us to pick up the weapons."},
{q:"Whose hands did Elisha lay upon the king's hands?", options:["His own hands","The hands of his servant","The hands of the captains","The hands of the priests"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 13:16",verse:"And he said to the king of Israel, Put thine hand upon the bow. And he put his hand upon it: and Elisha put his hands upon the king’s hands.", insight:"Elisha's hands upon the king's hands; God's power works through yielded hands."},
{q:"Which way was the window opened before the king shot?", options:["Eastward","Westward","Northward","Toward Jerusalem"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 13:17",verse:"And he said, Open the window eastward. And he opened it. Then Elisha said, Shoot. And he shot. And he said, The arrow of the LORD’S deliverance, and the arrow of deliverance from Syria: for thou shalt smite the Syrians in Aphek, till thou have consumed them.", insight:"The window opened eastward, toward Syria; faith aims at the real enemy."},
{q:"What did the shot arrow signify?", options:["The arrow of the LORD's deliverance from Syria","The crowning of a new king","The coming of the Assyrians","The death of the prophet"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 13:17",verse:"And he said, Open the window eastward. And he opened it. Then Elisha said, Shoot. And he shot. And he said, The arrow of the LORD’S deliverance, and the arrow of deliverance from Syria: for thou shalt smite the Syrians in Aphek, till thou have consumed them.", insight:"The arrow of the LORD's deliverance; every victory over sin is God's arrow, not ours."},
{q:"How many times did the king smite upon the ground?", options:["Thrice","Once","Five times","Seven times"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 13:18",verse:"And he said, Take the arrows. And he took them. And he said unto the king of Israel, Smite upon the ground. And he smote thrice, and stayed.", insight:"He smote thrice, and stayed; half hearted obedience stops short of full victory."},
{q:"Why was the man of God wroth with the king?", options:["He smote only thrice instead of five or six times","He refused to shoot the arrow","He wept instead of fighting","He brought no offering"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 13:19",verse:"And the man of God was wroth with him, and said, Thou shouldest have smitten five or six times; then hadst thou smitten Syria till thou hadst consumed it: whereas now thou shalt smite Syria but thrice.", insight:"Five or six times would have consumed Syria; small faith gets small victories."},
{q:"Who invaded the land at the coming in of the year after Elisha died?", options:["Bands of the Moabites","The armies of Assyria","The Philistines of Gath","The Edomites"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 13:20",verse:"And Elisha died, and they buried him. And the bands of the Moabites invaded the land at the coming in of the year.", insight:"Elisha died and was buried; even prophets finish their course, but God's work goes on."},
{q:"What happened to the dead man cast into Elisha's sepulchre?", options:["He touched Elisha's bones, revived, and stood upon his feet","He was buried with honors","His bones were scattered","He was taken to Samaria"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 13:21",verse:"And it came to pass, as they were burying a man, that, behold, they spied a band of men; and they cast the man into the sepulchre of Elisha: and when the man was let down, and touched the bones of Elisha, he revived, and stood up on his feet.", insight:"A dead man lived at the touch of Elisha's bones; God's power outlives His servants."},
{q:"Why was the LORD gracious to oppressed Israel?", options:["Because of His covenant with Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob","Because of Jehoahaz's righteousness","Because of Elisha's prayers alone","Because Syria had repented"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 13:23",verse:"And the LORD was gracious unto them, and had compassion on them, and had respect unto them, because of his covenant with Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob, and would not destroy them, neither cast he them from his presence as yet.", insight:"Gracious because of the covenant with Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob; mercy flows from promise, not performance."},
{q:"How many times did Joash beat Ben-hadad and recover Israel's cities?", options:["Three times","Once","Seven times","Twelve times"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 13:25",verse:"And Jehoash the son of Jehoahaz took again out of the hand of Ben-hadad the son of Hazael the cities, which he had taken out of the hand of Jehoahaz his father by war. Three times did Joash beat him, and recovered the cities of Israel.", insight:"Three times Joash beat Ben-hadad; even limited obedience recovered real ground."}
]},
{n:14, name:"The Thistle and the Cedar", seal:{ref:"2 Kings 14:27",verse:"And the LORD said not that he would blot out the name of Israel from under heaven: but he saved them by the hand of Jeroboam the son of Joash."}, facts:["Did you know Amaziah spared the murderers' children, appealing to the law of Moses that every man dies for his own sin (2 Kings 14:6)?","Did you know Jehoash answered Amaziah's war challenge with a fable: a thistle demanding a cedar's daughter, trodden down by a wild beast (2 Kings 14:9)?","Did you know Jonah, the prophet of the great fish, first appears here, foretelling Jeroboam's restoration of Israel's borders from Hamath to the sea of the plain (2 Kings 14:25)?"], questions:[
{q:"How old was Amaziah when he began to reign, and how long did he reign?", options:["Twenty and five years old; reigned twenty and nine years","Sixteen years old; reigned fifty two years","Twenty and two years old; reigned sixteen years","Seven years old; reigned forty years"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 14:2",verse:"He was twenty and five years old when he began to reign, and reigned twenty and nine years in Jerusalem. And his mother’s name was Jehoaddan of Jerusalem.", insight:"Twenty five at the start, twenty nine years of rule; a long reign is a long stewardship."},
{q:"Who was the mother of Amaziah?", options:["Jehoaddan of Jerusalem","Zibiah of Beer-sheba","Jecholiah of Jerusalem","Athaliah of Samaria"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 14:2",verse:"He was twenty and five years old when he began to reign, and reigned twenty and nine years in Jerusalem. And his mother’s name was Jehoaddan of Jerusalem.", insight:"Jehoaddan of Jerusalem is named; behind every king stands a mother God remembers."},
{q:"How is Amaziah's reign described?", options:["Right in the sight of the LORD, yet not like David his father","Evil above all the kings before him","Perfect as the days of Solomon","Weak and fearful"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 14:3",verse:"And he did that which was right in the sight of the LORD, yet not like David his father: he did according to all things as Joash his father did.", insight:"Right, yet not like David; God measures us against wholeheartedness, not mere correctness."},
{q:"What did Amaziah do as soon as the kingdom was confirmed in his hand?", options:["He slew his servants which had slain the king his father","He made peace with Israel","He repaired the temple","He freed all the slaves"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 14:5",verse:"And it came to pass, as soon as the kingdom was confirmed in his hand, that he slew his servants which had slain the king his father.", insight:"He executed justice once his throne was secure; delayed justice is still owed justice."},
{q:"Why did Amaziah spare the children of the murderers?", options:["The law of Moses commands that every man die for his own sin","They were too young to know","The priests pleaded for them","He feared their families"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 14:6",verse:"But the children of the murderers he slew not: according unto that which is written in the book of the law of Moses, wherein the LORD commanded, saying, The fathers shall not be put to death for the children, nor the children be put to death for the fathers; but every man shall be put to death for his own sin.", insight:"Every man for his own sin; God refuses the sins of the fathers as an excuse or a charge."},
{q:"How many Edomites did Amaziah slay in the valley of salt?", options:["Ten thousand","Twenty thousand","Five thousand","One thousand"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 14:7",verse:"He slew of Edom in the valley of salt ten thousand, and took Selah by war, and called the name of it Joktheel unto this day.", insight:"Ten thousand Edomites in the valley of salt; God gave the victory, and pride took the credit."},
{q:"What did Amaziah rename the city of Selah after taking it by war?", options:["Joktheel","Jehovah-jireh","Amaziah's rock","Petra"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 14:7",verse:"He slew of Edom in the valley of salt ten thousand, and took Selah by war, and called the name of it Joktheel unto this day.", insight:"Selah became Joktheel; new names mark new seasons, but only humility keeps them."},
{q:"What challenge did Amaziah send to Jehoash king of Israel?", options:["Come, let us look one another in the face","Meet me at the temple gate","Send tribute to Jerusalem","Join me against Edom"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 14:8",verse:"Then Amaziah sent messengers to Jehoash, the son of Jehoahaz son of Jehu, king of Israel, saying, Come, let us look one another in the face.", insight:"'Let us look one another in the face' was a challenge, not a greeting; pride dresses for war as friendship."},
{q:"In Jehoash's parable, what did the thistle ask of the cedar?", options:["Give thy daughter to my son to wife","Give me thy timber for building","Bow down before the forest","Lend me thy roots"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 14:9",verse:"And Jehoash the king of Israel sent to Amaziah king of Judah, saying, The thistle that was in Lebanon sent to the cedar that was in Lebanon, saying, Give thy daughter to my son to wife: and there passed by a wild beast that was in Lebanon, and trode down the thistle.", insight:"A thistle demanding a cedar's daughter; pride always overestimates its own height."},
{q:"What trode down the thistle in the parable?", options:["A wild beast in Lebanon","A flood from the mountains","A fire from heaven","An axe of the woodman"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 14:9",verse:"And Jehoash the king of Israel sent to Amaziah king of Judah, saying, The thistle that was in Lebanon sent to the cedar that was in Lebanon, saying, Give thy daughter to my son to wife: and there passed by a wild beast that was in Lebanon, and trode down the thistle.", insight:"The wild beast trode down the thistle; the proud are crushed by forces they never noticed."},
{q:"What counsel did Jehoash give the proud Amaziah?", options:["Glory of thy victory over Edom, and tarry at home","Gather a greater army","Sacrifice to the LORD first","Flee to Egypt"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 14:10",verse:"Thou hast indeed smitten Edom, and thine heart hath lifted thee up: glory of this, and tarry at home: for why shouldest thou meddle to thy hurt, that thou shouldest fall, even thou, and Judah with thee?", insight:"'Tarry at home' was wise counsel from an enemy; God can speak warning through unlikely mouths."},
{q:"Where did the two kings look one another in the face?", options:["At Beth-shemesh, which belongeth to Judah","At Megiddo","In the valley of salt","At the gates of Samaria"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 14:11",verse:"But Amaziah would not hear. Therefore Jehoash king of Israel went up; and he and Amaziah king of Judah looked one another in the face at Beth-shemesh, which belongeth to Judah.", insight:"They met at Beth-shemesh; the field of pride becomes the field of defeat."},
{q:"What became of Judah's army?", options:["Judah was put to the worse, and they fled every man to their tents","It stood firm all the day","It captured Samaria","It joined with Israel"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 14:12",verse:"And Judah was put to the worse before Israel; and they fled every man to their tents.", insight:"Judah fled every man to his tent; when leaders fall, the people scatter."},
{q:"How much of Jerusalem's wall did Jehoash break down?", options:["Four hundred cubits, from the gate of Ephraim to the corner gate","Two hundred cubits by the water gate","The whole wall round about","Only the corner gate"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 14:13",verse:"And Jehoash king of Israel took Amaziah king of Judah, the son of Jehoash the son of Ahaziah, at Beth-shemesh, and came to Jerusalem, and brake down the wall of Jerusalem from the gate of Ephraim unto the corner gate, four hundred cubits.", insight:"Four hundred cubits of wall broken; pride's wars leave the city exposed."},
{q:"What did Jehoash carry back to Samaria?", options:["All the gold and silver, the vessels of the house of the LORD, and hostages","Only the temple singers","The ark and the tables","Prisoners of Edom"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 14:14",verse:"And he took all the gold and silver, and all the vessels that were found in the house of the LORD, and in the treasures of the king’s house, and hostages, and returned to Samaria.", insight:"Gold, silver, vessels, hostages to Samaria; one proud challenge cost Judah its treasures."},
{q:"Where did Amaziah flee from the conspiracy, and where was he slain?", options:["He fled to Lachish, and was slain at Lachish","He fled to Egypt, and died there","He fled to Samaria, and was slain there","He hid in the temple, and was slain there"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 14:19",verse:"Now they made a conspiracy against him in Jerusalem: and he fled to Lachish; but they sent after him to Lachish, and slew him there.", insight:"He fled to Lachish but could not outrun the conspiracy; no distance escapes the fruit of pride."},
{q:"How old was Azariah when the people of Judah made him king?", options:["Sixteen years old","Twenty and five years old","Seven years old","Twenty years old"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 14:21",verse:"And all the people of Judah took Azariah, which was sixteen years old, and made him king instead of his father Amaziah.", insight:"Sixteen years old and made king; God raises new leaders from the ruins of the old."},
{q:"How long did Jeroboam the son of Joash reign over Israel in Samaria?", options:["Forty and one years","Sixteen years","Seventeen years","Fifty two years"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 14:23",verse:"In the fifteenth year of Amaziah the son of Joash king of Judah Jeroboam the son of Joash king of Israel began to reign in Samaria, and reigned forty and one years.", insight:"Forty one years of an evil king's reign; God can use even a wicked reign to show mercy."},
{q:"By whose word did Jeroboam restore Israel's coast from Hamath to the sea of the plain?", options:["Jonah the son of Amittai, of Gath-hepher","Elisha the prophet","Isaiah the son of Amoz","Elijah the Tishbite"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 14:25",verse:"He restored the coast of Israel from the entering of Hamath unto the sea of the plain, according to the word of the LORD God of Israel, which he spake by the hand of his servant Jonah, the son of Amittai, the prophet, which was of Gath-hepher.", insight:"Jonah's word restored the coast from Hamath to the sea of the plain; God's prophets shape nations, not just fish stories."},
{q:"Why did the LORD save Israel by the hand of Jeroboam?", options:["He had not said He would blot out Israel's name, and He saw their bitter affliction","Jeroboam was righteous","The people had repented","The prophets had interceded"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 14:27",verse:"And the LORD said not that he would blot out the name of Israel from under heaven: but he saved them by the hand of Jeroboam the son of Joash.", insight:"God had not said He would blot out Israel's name; mercy, not merit, kept the nation alive."}
]},
{n:15, name:"Crowns in Turmoil", seal:{ref:"2 Kings 15:12",verse:"This was the word of the LORD which he spake unto Jehu, saying, Thy sons shall sit on the throne of Israel unto the fourth generation. And so it came to pass."}, facts:["Did you know this single chapter records the fall of five kings of Israel in rapid succession: Zachariah murdered, Shallum slain after a month, Pekahiah conspired against, and Pekah conspired against, each crown passing by the sword (2 Kings 15:10-30)?","Did you know God's promise to Jehu was kept to the exact generation: his sons sat on Israel's throne unto the fourth generation, and 'so it came to pass' (2 Kings 15:12)?","Did you know Menahem taxed every wealthy man in Israel fifty shekels of silver to raise the thousand talents that bought off Pul of Assyria (2 Kings 15:19-20)?"], questions:[
{q:"How old was Azariah when he began to reign, and how long did he reign?", options:["Sixteen years old; reigned two and fifty years","Twenty and five years old; reigned twenty nine years","Seven years old; reigned forty years","Twenty years old; reigned sixteen years"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 15:2",verse:"Sixteen years old was he when he began to reign, and he reigned two and fifty years in Jerusalem. And his mother’s name was Jecholiah of Jerusalem.", insight:"Sixteen years old, fifty two years of reign; a lifetime on the throne tests the heart daily."},
{q:"What did the LORD do to King Azariah?", options:["He smote him, so he was a leper unto the day of his death","He gave him a son in his old age","He delivered him from Assyria","He doubled his kingdom"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 15:5",verse:"And the LORD smote the king, so that he was a leper unto the day of his death, and dwelt in a several house. And Jotham the king’s son was over the house, judging the people of the land.", insight:"Smitten a leper unto the day of his death; even kings are not above God's correction."},
{q:"Where did the leprous king dwell?", options:["In a several house, apart","In the temple court","In the palace at Samaria","In a tent at Lachish"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 15:5",verse:"And the LORD smote the king, so that he was a leper unto the day of his death, and dwelt in a several house. And Jotham the king’s son was over the house, judging the people of the land.", insight:"He dwelt in a several house; sin isolates, even in a palace."},
{q:"Who reigned in Judah after Azariah slept with his fathers?", options:["Jotham his son","Ahaz his son","Zachariah of Israel","Pekahiah of Israel"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 15:7",verse:"So Azariah slept with his fathers; and they buried him with his fathers in the city of David: and Jotham his son reigned in his stead.", insight:"Jotham reigned in his stead; God keeps the line going when a king is set aside."},
{q:"How long did Zachariah the son of Jeroboam reign in Samaria?", options:["Six months","One full month","Two years","Ten years"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 15:8",verse:"In the thirty and eighth year of Azariah king of Judah did Zachariah the son of Jeroboam reign over Israel in Samaria six months.", insight:"Six months on the throne; a dynasty built on blood ends quickly."},
{q:"Who conspired against Zachariah and slew him?", options:["Shallum the son of Jabesh","Menahem the son of Gadi","Pekah the son of Remaliah","Hoshea the son of Elah"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 15:10",verse:"And Shallum the son of Jabesh conspired against him, and smote him before the people, and slew him, and reigned in his stead.", insight:"Shallum smote him before the people; public murder breeds public instability."},
{q:"What word of the LORD to Jehu came to pass in Zachariah's death?", options:["Thy sons shall sit on the throne of Israel unto the fourth generation","The house of Ahab shall utterly perish","Jezreel shall be avenged","The calves of Bethel shall be broken"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 15:12",verse:"This was the word of the LORD which he spake unto Jehu, saying, Thy sons shall sit on the throne of Israel unto the fourth generation. And so it came to pass.", insight:"'And so it came to pass'; God's word about Jehu's house was kept to the generation."},
{q:"How long did Shallum reign in Samaria?", options:["A full month","Six months","Two years","Twenty years"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 15:13",verse:"Shallum the son of Jabesh began to reign in the nine and thirtieth year of Uzziah king of Judah; and he reigned a full month in Samaria.", insight:"A full month was all; thrones seized by conspiracy rarely hold."},
{q:"Who went up from Tirzah and slew Shallum in Samaria?", options:["Menahem the son of Gadi","Pekah the son of Remaliah","Hoshea the son of Elah","Tiglath-pileser"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 15:14",verse:"For Menahem the son of Gadi went up from Tirzah, and came to Samaria, and smote Shallum the son of Jabesh in Samaria, and slew him, and reigned in his stead.", insight:"Menahem went up from Tirzah to slay; violence begets violence in a godless kingdom."},
{q:"Why did Menahem smite Tiphsah?", options:["Because they opened not to him","Because it worshipped Baal","Because it sheltered Shallum","Because Assyria commanded it"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 15:16",verse:"Then Menahem smote Tiphsah, and all that were therein, and the coasts thereof from Tirzah: because they opened not to him, therefore he smote it; and all the women therein that were with child he ripped up.", insight:"They opened not, so he smote; cruelty in war reveals a heart without mercy."},
{q:"How long did Menahem reign over Israel?", options:["Ten years","Twenty years","Two years","Six months"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 15:17",verse:"In the nine and thirtieth year of Azariah king of Judah began Menahem the son of Gadi to reign over Israel, and reigned ten years in Samaria.", insight:"Ten years of an evil reign; length without righteousness is just a longer fall."},
{q:"Which king of Assyria came against the land in Menahem's days?", options:["Pul","Tiglath-pileser","Shalmaneser","Sennacherib"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 15:19",verse:"And Pul the king of Assyria came against the land: and Menahem gave Pul a thousand talents of silver, that his hand might be with him to confirm the kingdom in his hand.", insight:"Pul came against the land; when God is forgotten, empires come collecting."},
{q:"How much silver did Menahem give Pul to confirm his kingdom?", options:["A thousand talents of silver","Fifty shekels of silver","Ten talents of gold","Three hundred shields of gold"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 15:19",verse:"And Pul the king of Assyria came against the land: and Menahem gave Pul a thousand talents of silver, that his hand might be with him to confirm the kingdom in his hand.", insight:"A thousand talents to confirm his kingdom; bought thrones are never secure."},
{q:"How did Menahem raise the tribute money?", options:["He exacted fifty shekels of silver from each mighty man of wealth","He emptied the temple treasury","He sold Israelites as slaves","He borrowed from Tyre"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 15:20",verse:"And Menahem exacted the money of Israel, even of all the mighty men of wealth, of each man fifty shekels of silver, to give to the king of Assyria. So the king of Assyria turned back, and stayed not there in the land.", insight:"Fifty shekels from every wealthy man; the people's wealth paid for the king's fear."},
{q:"How long did Pekahiah the son of Menahem reign in Samaria?", options:["Two years","Ten years","Twenty years","Six months"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 15:23",verse:"In the fiftieth year of Azariah king of Judah Pekahiah the son of Menahem began to reign over Israel in Samaria, and reigned two years.", insight:"Two years, then the sword; short reigns follow the same sins."},
{q:"Who conspired against Pekahiah in the palace of the king's house?", options:["Pekah the son of Remaliah, his captain, with fifty Gileadites","Shallum the son of Jabesh","Hoshea the son of Elah","Argob and Arieh alone"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 15:25",verse:"But Pekah the son of Remaliah, a captain of his, conspired against him, and smote him in Samaria, in the palace of the king’s house, with Argob and Arieh, and with him fifty men of the Gileadites: and he killed him, and reigned in his room.", insight:"A captain with fifty Gileadites in the palace; trusted men make the deadliest conspirators."},
{q:"How long did Pekah the son of Remaliah reign over Israel?", options:["Twenty years","Ten years","Two years","Sixteen years"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 15:27",verse:"In the two and fiftieth year of Azariah king of Judah Pekah the son of Remaliah began to reign over Israel in Samaria, and reigned twenty years.", insight:"Twenty years of the same evil; time does not reform a heart set on sin."},
{q:"Which places did Tiglath-pileser take and carry captive to Assyria?", options:["Ijon, Abel-beth-maachah, Janoah, Kedesh, Hazor, Gilead, Galilee, and Naphtali","Samaria and Jerusalem","Tyre and Sidon","Damascus and Hamath"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 15:29",verse:"In the days of Pekah king of Israel came Tiglath-pileser king of Assyria, and took Ijon, and Abel-beth-maachah, and Janoah, and Kedesh, and Hazor, and Gilead, and Galilee, all the land of Naphtali, and carried them captive to Assyria.", insight:"City after city carried captive to Assyria; the exile began long before Samaria fell."},
{q:"Who made a conspiracy against Pekah and reigned in his stead?", options:["Hoshea the son of Elah","Shallum the son of Jabesh","Menahem the son of Gadi","Rezin of Syria"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 15:30",verse:"And Hoshea the son of Elah made a conspiracy against Pekah the son of Remaliah, and smote him, and slew him, and reigned in his stead, in the twentieth year of Jotham the son of Uzziah.", insight:"Hoshea conspired and reigned; the last king of Israel took the throne the same way the others lost it."},
{q:"What did Jotham build?", options:["The higher gate of the house of the LORD","A new palace at Jerusalem","The walls of Lachish","A tower in the wilderness"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 15:35",verse:"Howbeit the high places were not removed: the people sacrificed and burned incense still in the high places. He built the higher gate of the house of the LORD.", insight:"He built the higher gate of the house of the LORD; even in dark days, some build for God."}
]}
]);
